From 83a1e0ba06235e55d1c411a8888fbc172760e14a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:46:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/mediatek: order MT6897 display runtime PM ownership

Hold the MMSYS devices used by an active CRTC, including the shared DRM parent, before starting the path. Use the controller order for acquisition and reverse it after checked stop. Replace follower links only for this variant.

Pin the actual component, mutex, supplier and parent closure during teardown so its existing asynchronous puts cannot become final before the consumer-first drain. Preserve other owners and retain still-owned resources on failure.

Link: https://github.com/MiCode/MTK_kernel_device_modules/blob/3c4ccd07d5624879555ec710c11bb8818e5cb5c6/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mediatek_v2/mtk_drm_drv.c#L5554-L5641

Link: https://github.com/MiCode/MTK_kernel_device_modules/blob/3c4ccd07d5624879555ec710c11bb8818e5cb5c6/drivers/gpu/drm/mediatek/mediatek_v2/mtk_drm_drv.c#L5734-L5813
Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
